===GAME START===
INT. MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY - DAY

Holden steps into the museum, the familiar scent of polished wood and old exhibits enveloping him. He gazes at the towering dinosaur skeletons, feeling a sense of comfort wash over him.

HOLDEN
(to himself)
This place... it never changes. 

He wanders through the halls, stopping at a display of ancient artifacts. Memories of childhood visits flood back, and he feels a bittersweet nostalgia.

HOLDEN
(softly)
I wish things could be like this again.

As he stands in front of a glass case, he reflects on his life, the chaos outside fading away. The stillness of the museum allows him to confront his feelings of isolation.

HOLDEN
(whispering)
Maybe there’s still hope for me...

With a renewed sense of purpose, he smiles slightly, feeling a spark of authenticity ignite within him.

===GAME END===

